{
  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (RNA-only, single-profile, PCA n2000) achieves 0.485 acc, and config_016 (multimodal, single-profile, PCA n2000+ResNet50, concat) improves to 0.527, confirming RNA is the dominant signal and image adds a modest boost. However, we have no evidence yet on whether multiprofile with aggregation improves over single-profile—a fundamental architectural choice that halves the remaining configuration space. Question: config_002 (RNA-only, multiprofile, PCA n2000, avgpool) is a clean single-variable comparison to config_001, isolating the effect of multiprofile+avgpool aggregation while holding the RNA encoder constant. Why this is best: It is the simplest, cheapest experiment that directly answers whether the multiprofile/aggregation axis is worth pursuing. If it improves over config_001, we gain confidence to extend multiprofile into the multimodal setting (e.g., config_018/020). If it does not help, we can deprioritize all multiprofile variants and focus budget on RNA encoder or image encoder choices in the single-profile regime. This maximizes information per experiment under the limited budget."
}

